            </note>
            <note corresp="#d24-f4" n="4" xml:id="d24-f4-content">
                <p>In a March 31 note to Secretary Rusk,
                    attached to another copy of his memorandum of March 26, McGeorge Bundy wrote: “The action referred to
                    in paragraph 3 of this memorandum will await the completion of the Joint Staff
                    studies which Secretary McNamara
                    mentioned at a recent luncheon meeting with the President.” (National Archives
                    and Records Administration, RG 59, Central Files
                    1964–66, DEF 12 US)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d24-f5" n="5" xml:id="d24-f5-content">
